      <activity id="ad389de7-fc69-5270-b0e7-3f9013506978" activityNameId="2df7cd2e-9594-5764-a666-c7d0cbd1dfb7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Pentane, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Pentane, at plant
Data are from the Eco-profiles of the European plastics industry (PlasticsEurope). Not included are the values reported for: recyclable wastes, amount of air / N2 / O2 consumed, unspecified metal emission to air and to water, mercaptan emission to air, unspecified CFC/HCFC emission to air, dioxin to water. The amount of "sulphur (bonded)" is assumed to be included into the amount of raw oil.;
CAS number: 000109-66-0; 
Synonyms: amyl hydride, n-pentane, n-Pentan, skellysolve; 
UUID: 2b89ce00-c1f2-3e3e-b822-550b42aa88c2
Aggregated data for all processes from raw material extraction until delivery at plant
Location: different European production sites
Technology: production 90% by cracking or reforming processes in a refinery out of gasoline or naphtha fractions / 10% as by-product
Time period: time to which data refer
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature values based on company survey 
Extrapolations: no extrapolation
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2b89ce00-c1f2-3e3e-b822-550b42aa88c2.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
